Use the installed Windows SDK instead of hardcoded SDK 8.0 paths.

build/common.gypi dates from 2014 and wires Windows SDK 8.0 locations straight
into the compiler and linker settings:

  * windows_sdk_path defaults to 'C:/Program Files (x86)/Windows Kits/8.0'
    (the detected fallback, third_party/platformsdk_win8, is not fetched).
  * Include dirs are '<sdk>/Include/{shared,um,winrt}'. SDK 10 nests those
    under a version directory, and adds 'ucrt', which did not exist yet.
  * Library dirs are '<sdk>/Lib/win8/um/<arch>'. SDK 10 uses
    'Lib/<version>/um/<arch>'.

On a VS2022 machine none of those paths exist. They are prepended to the real
ones, so cl and link silently ignore them -- but they are wrong, they mask
which SDK is actually in use, and they are what the VS project migrator
complains about ("could not convert attribute AdditionalLibraryDirectories...
Windows Kits\8.0\Lib\win8\um\x86").

GYP's msvs generator emits WindowsTargetPlatformVersion, so MSBuild's own
toolset property sheets resolve the SDK and ATL include/library paths
correctly. This drops the hardcoded entries and lets that happen.

The variable definition itself is left in place; nothing references it now.

--- a/build/common.gypi
+++ b/build/common.gypi
@@ -2903,18 +2903,13 @@
         'msvs_settings': {
           'VCLinkerTool': {
             'TargetMachine': '17', # x86 - 64
-            'AdditionalLibraryDirectories!':
-              ['<(windows_sdk_path)/Lib/win8/um/x86'],
-            'AdditionalLibraryDirectories':
-              ['<(windows_sdk_path)/Lib/win8/um/x64'],
+            # PATCHED: SDK 8.0 'Lib/win8/um/<arch>' paths dropped; MSBuild
+            # resolves the SDK libraries from WindowsTargetPlatformVersion.
             # Doesn't exist x64 SDK. Should use oleaut32 in any case.
             'IgnoreDefaultLibraryNames': [ 'olepro32.lib' ],
           },
           'VCLibrarianTool': {
-            'AdditionalLibraryDirectories!':
-              ['<(windows_sdk_path)/Lib/win8/um/x86'],
-            'AdditionalLibraryDirectories':
-              ['<(windows_sdk_path)/Lib/win8/um/x64'],
+            # PATCHED: see above.
             'TargetMachine': '17', # x64
           },
         },
@@ -4945,10 +4940,14 @@
           }],
         ],
         'msvs_system_include_dirs': [
-          '<(windows_sdk_path)/Include/shared',
-          '<(windows_sdk_path)/Include/um',
-          '<(windows_sdk_path)/Include/winrt',
-          '$(VSInstallDir)/VC/atlmfc/include',
+          # PATCHED: these pointed into Windows SDK 8.0, whose layout
+          # ('Include/shared' etc. directly under the SDK root) no longer
+          # matches SDK 10, and which has no 'ucrt' entry because the
+          # Universal CRT postdates this file. '$(VSInstallDir)/VC/atlmfc'
+          # likewise moved under VC/Tools/MSVC in VS2017.
+          #
+          # GYP sets WindowsTargetPlatformVersion, so MSBuild's own toolset
+          # property sheets supply the correct SDK and ATL include paths.
         ],
         'msvs_cygwin_shell': 0,
         'msvs_disabled_warnings': [4351, 4355, 4396, 4503, 4819,
@@ -4978,9 +4977,7 @@
           },
           'VCLibrarianTool': {
             'AdditionalOptions': ['/ignore:4221'],
-            'AdditionalLibraryDirectories': [
-              '<(windows_sdk_path)/Lib/win8/um/x86',
-            ],
+            # PATCHED: SDK 8.0 library path dropped; see above.
           },
           'VCLinkerTool': {
             'AdditionalDependencies': [
@@ -4995,9 +4992,7 @@
               'winmm.lib',
               'shlwapi.lib',
             ],
-            'AdditionalLibraryDirectories': [
-              '<(windows_sdk_path)/Lib/win8/um/x86',
-            ],
+            # PATCHED: SDK 8.0 library path dropped; see above.
             'GenerateDebugInformation': 'true',
             'MapFileName': '$(OutDir)\\$(TargetName).map',
             'ImportLibrary': '$(OutDir)\\lib\\$(TargetName).lib',
